<h3 id=3D"why-did-usage-go-up-after-the-new-model-launched" class=3D"mt-8 s=
croll-mt-5 text-[18px] leading-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text=
-(--Labels-Primary)">Why did usage go up after the new model launched?</h3>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)">After =
switching models, the context cache built earlier no longer hits on the new=
 model, so that context has to be re-prefilled. Usage therefore looks highe=
r right after switching. Recommended action:</p>
<ul class=3D"pl-4 text-(--Labels-Primary) [&amp;&gt;li]:mt-2 [&amp;&gt;li]:=
relative [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-4 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:bef=
ore:left-0 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:top-[11px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:h-[6px] [&a=
mp;&gt;li]:before:w-[6px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:rounded-full [&amp;&gt;li]:b=
efore:bg-current">
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>Start a new session when u=
sing the new model</strong>: this gives better results and lower consumptio=
n.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"why-do-i-still-get-a-401-with-the-correct-model-id" class=3D"mt-8=
 scroll-mt-5 text-[18px] leading-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] te=
xt-(--Labels-Primary)">Why do I still get a 401 with the correct model ID?<=
/h3>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)">When t=
he requested capability exceeds your plan's entitlements, the server return=
s <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center rounded-[4px] px-2 py-0=
 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">401</code>. Three common cases:</p>
<ul class=3D"pl-4 text-(--Labels-Primary) [&amp;&gt;li]:mt-2 [&amp;&gt;li]:=
relative [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-4 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:bef=
ore:left-0 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:top-[11px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:h-[6px] [&a=
mp;&gt;li]:before:w-[6px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:rounded-full [&amp;&gt;li]:b=
efore:bg-current">
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>No K3 access</strong>: you=
r plan is below Moderato / Plus and can't call <code class=3D"inline-flex l=
eading-6 items-center rounded-[4px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-in=
k)">k3</code>, <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center rounded-[4=
px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">k3-256k</code> (the new Go t=
ier has no coding quota) =E2=80=94 upgrade to Moderato / Plus or above.</li=
>
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>No 1M access</strong>: on =
a Moderato / Plus plan, <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center r=
ounded-[4px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">k3</code> supports =
up to 256K context; up to 1M context is available on Allegretto / Pro or ab=
ove. <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center rounded-[4px] px-2 p=
y-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">k3-256k</code> has a fixed 256K contex=
t limit.</li>
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>No HighSpeed access</stron=
g>: some plans don't include HighSpeed =E2=80=94 upgrade to Allegretto / Pr=
o or above to call <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center rounde=
d-[4px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">kimi-for-coding-highspee=
d</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)">For th=
e full error text and how to handle it, see the <a class=3D"leading-7 text-=
(--Colors-KMBlue) decoration-(--hc-pill-border) decoration-2 transition-col=
ors hover:text-(--Colors-KMBlue-hover)" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/en/hel=
p/kimi-code/error-reference">Error Reference</a>.</p>
<h3 id=3D"why-isnt-highspeed-noticeably-faster" class=3D"mt-8 scroll-mt-5 t=
ext-[18px] leading-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-(--Labels-P=
rimary)">Why isn't HighSpeed noticeably faster?</h3>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)">Two co=
mmon reasons:</p>
<ul class=3D"pl-4 text-(--Labels-Primary) [&amp;&gt;li]:mt-2 [&amp;&gt;li]:=
relative [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-4 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:bef=
ore:left-0 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:top-[11px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:h-[6px] [&a=
mp;&gt;li]:before:w-[6px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:rounded-full [&amp;&gt;li]:b=
efore:bg-current">
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>Mistyped model ID</strong>=
: the HighSpeed ID must be <code class=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-cente=
r rounded-[4px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fills-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">kimi-for-coding-=
highspeed</code>; a wrong value silently falls back to the standard <code c=
lass=3D"inline-flex leading-6 items-center rounded-[4px] px-2 py-0 bg-(--Fi=
lls-F2) text-(--hc-ink)">kimi-for-coding</code> =E2=80=94 no error, no spee=
dup.</li>
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]"><strong>Tools and scripts dominate=
</strong>: HighSpeed only speeds up <strong>model output</strong>. Tool cal=
ls (reading/writing files, running commands, etc.) and script execution are=
 unaffected, so when they take up most of a turn the overall speedup feels =
small.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"how-to-reduce-the-overhead-of-switching-reasoning-" class=3D"mt-8=
 scroll-mt-5 text-[18px] leading-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] te=
xt-(--Labels-Primary)">How to reduce the overhead of switching reasoning ef=
fort?</h3>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)">Switch=
ing reasoning effort invalidates the context cache you've built up, so cont=
ext that would have hit the cache must be re-prefilled. To avoid triggering=
 re-prefill too often:</p>
<ul class=3D"pl-4 text-(--Labels-Primary) [&amp;&gt;li]:mt-2 [&amp;&gt;li]:=
relative [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-4 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:absolute [&amp;&gt;li]:bef=
ore:left-0 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:top-[11px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:h-[6px] [&a=
mp;&gt;li]:before:w-[6px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:rounded-full [&amp;&gt;li]:b=
efore:bg-current">
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]">Pick an effort that fits the task =
and keep it consistent within a session;</li>
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]">When you genuinely need a differen=
t effort, start a new session rather than switching back and forth in a lon=
g session.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"switching-between-k3-1m-and-k3-256k" class=3D"mt-8 scroll-mt-5 te=
xt-[18px] leading-[28px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-(--Labels-Pr=
imary)">Switching between K3 (1M) and K3-256k</h3>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)"><stron=
g>Switching from K3 (1M) to K3-256k</strong>: if the current session's cont=
ext already exceeds 256k, some coding tools (such as Kimi Code CLI and Clau=
de Code) will perform a compact on the tool side. Recommendations:</p>
<ol class=3D"list-decimal pl-8 text-(--Labels-Primary) marker:font-semibold=
 marker:text-[18px] [&amp;&gt;li]:mt-2 [&amp;_ul]:list-[circle] [&amp;_ul]:=
pl-4 [&amp;_ul&gt;li]:pl-0 [&amp;_ul&gt;li]:before:hidden">
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]">Manually run compact once before s=
witching to compress the context to within 256k. This preserves the key poi=
nts of the task, keeps the session intact, and lets you benefit from more d=
urable quota after switching.</li>
<li class=3D"text-[18px] leading-[28px]">If the conversation history includ=
es video files, switching directly will fail because K3-256k does not suppo=
rt video input. Please compact first, then switch.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"mt-4 text-[18px] leading-[26px] text-(--Labels-Primary)"><stron=
g>Switching from K3-256k to K3 (1M)</strong>: if <code class=3D"inline-flex=
